# Workflow plan step W6 (docs/WORKFLOW_PLAN.md, 2026-11-14): sanity checks after a run, shown on Results only when they fail.
# The cavity read into Setup and run for 0.05 s: under one flow-through (0.1 m at 1 m/s takes 0.1 s). pitzDaily read into
# Setup, switched to laminar and run 30 iterations: Re far above turbulent, and its numbers still changing.
open $SB/ws/cavity
wait 10
click wf-next
wait-until job finished timeout 60
wait 10
click nav:physics
wait 10
click phys-adopt
wait 20
shell foamDictionary system/controlDict -entry endTime -set 0.05 > /dev/null && foamDictionary system/controlDict -entry writeInterval -set 5 > /dev/null
wait 120
click nav:run
wait-until page Run
click run-go
wait-until job running timeout 60
wait-until job finished timeout 120
wait 30
click nav:results
wait-until page Results
wait 30
assert text The run covers 0.5 flow-throughs
screenshot $OUT/w6_flowthrough.png
open $SB/ws/pitzDaily
wait 10
click wf-next
wait-until job finished timeout 60
wait 10
click nav:physics
wait 10
click phys-adopt
wait 20
click su-appr#0
wait 10
click su-write
wait 30
shell foamDictionary system/controlDict -entry endTime -set 30 > /dev/null && foamDictionary system/controlDict -entry writeInterval -set 10 > /dev/null && foamDictionary system/controlDict -entry functions -set '{ inFlow { type surfaceFieldValue; libs (fieldFunctionObjects); regionType patch; name inlet; operation sum; fields (phi); writeFields false; writeControl timeStep; } }' > /dev/null
wait 120
click nav:run
wait-until page Run
click run-go
wait-until job running timeout 60
wait-until job finished timeout 180
wait 30
click nav:results
wait-until page Results
wait 30
assert text A laminar model on a turbulent flow
screenshot $OUT/w6_laminar.png
